00:25:57,200 --> 00:26:01,760
Like your main gig will always destroy anything you try to do.

364
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:02,640
Yeah.

365
00:26:02,880 --> 00:26:16,400
So like an hour into my app launch and I didn't know what the news would be, but an hour into the launch before I even had a chance to like tweet it from the company account before even some of my own launch day plans were finished.

366
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:17,680
Apple announced that.

367
00:26:17,920 --> 00:26:29,440
And then I was like all hands on deck with you and Jacob and everybody else at RevenueCat trying to figure it out and then scheduling a we webinar for the very next day and like reading through all the documents and chatting about it internally.

368
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:39,040
And so what would have been maybe otherwise a lighter revenue cat day where I take a little personal time to celebrate my app launch was just complete decimate.

369
00:26:39,200 --> 00:26:46,480
So instead I was up till like two hours a day reading the fine print of European regulation to host a webinar the very next day.

370
00:26:47,120 --> 00:26:54,880
It was just about as big of a disaster as you could possibly have when your plan is to get attention.

371
00:26:55,120 --> 00:27:00,160
Apple still hasn't featured and I'm not totally sure why, but I have a feeling it's that well two things.

372
00:27:00,720 --> 00:27:09,920
And this is a regret that I have now, looking back, is I was trying to squeeze it in ahead of Vision Pro, and I thought so much air was going to be sucked out of the room from Vision Pro.

373
00:27:10,640 --> 00:27:23,680
What I didn't know was Apple was distracted with the DMA, but the whole editorial team was, I'm sure, so busy with the launch of the Vision Pro, I never could have known that the DMA would be such a big deal and would be launched on that day.

374
00:27:24,400 --> 00:27:29,040
But I should have known that the App Store editorial team would be super busy with the Vision Pro.

375
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:38,480
And the reason I was trying to get it out was to launch, was to like actually ship versus, oh, now we need to build a V Vision Pro app before we can ship.

376
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:43,360
And so I was trying to get out before the Vision Pro so that people were not asking, Well, where is your Vision Pro app or whatever?

377
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:47,840
Well, it turns out a month later, I don't think anyone would ask for a Vision Pro app anyway.

378
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:54,800
So, hindsight 2020, I should have just waited a month and let the Vision Pro stuff blow over before launching.

379
00:27:54,960 --> 00:28:00,800
But that's a top tip, subclub listeners, if you're going to launch your app, don't do it on the day that Apple announces the DMA.

380
00:28:01,200 --> 00:28:03,360
So take that one, write that one down in your mailbox.

381
00:28:03,520 --> 00:28:04,800
This is really actionable.

382
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:06,480
This applies to all businesses.

383
00:28:07,040 --> 00:28:07,600
You'll do better.

384
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,000
Yeah.

385
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:11,840
If you choose a different day than the day that the App Store melts down in Europe.

386
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:14,640
But it's another side effect of the big launch.

387
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:19,600
If you put all your eggs into one big launch basket, you're sometimes you're just going to catch a lost track.

388
00:28:19,840 --> 00:28:21,200
Some big news articles are going to come out.

389
00:28:21,200 --> 00:28:22,480
It happens with fundraisings too.

